 "seat": {
  "BEST_WHY": "The corridor running north from the figure (x\u2248378\u2013440, y 70\u2013460) is authored, not stamped. The joints are drawn as broken stipple \u2014 dotted, interrupted runs \u2014 rather than continuous lines, so the blocks read as chipped edges meeting badly. Block lengths vary along a single course (roughly 20, 35, 28, 45 px in the wall run at y\u2248390\u2013422), and two long cracks cross the corridor diagonally at y\u2248310 and y\u2248360, running *through* several joints without breaking at them \u2014 a crack that ignores block boundaries can only be hand-placed, and it is the single clearest tell in the deck that a person drew this. The dark vertical members at x\u2248565 and x\u2248660 break their course cleanly and read as driven timber. The falloff is monotonic and unbanded: down the corridor centre the luma climbs 9 \u2192 90 from y=200 to y=490 with no tile-step in it. And the sprite reads: the shield's cream face and the pale blade sit on floor at luma \u224890, so both hold.",
  "WORST_WHY": "Three separate failures, any one of which is disqualifying.\n\n*The dirt is stamped on a visible lattice.* Hashing the frame at 16 px shows the identical tile recurring 15 times at (160,0), (112,48), (160,48), (208,48), (64,96), (112,96)\u2026 \u2014 every coordinate 48 apart in both axes. The entire brown field is one 48\u00d748 patch repeated on an exact 3\u00d73-tile grid, and the same cluster of maroon splotches comes back every third tile.\n\n*Two camera angles in one frame.* The floor and water are straight top-down; the barrels at x\u2248112\u2013148 and x\u2248160\u2013196 show their lid ellipse *and* their front staves, so they are three-quarter; and the green figure at x\u2248206\u2013238, y 0\u201330 is full front elevation \u2014 you see its face, both eyes, its chest and both legs from the front, standing upright at the camera. Under it is a soft airbrushed brown ellipse, the only shadow anywhere in the frame, and it is a blurred blob rather than a pixel shape.\n\n*The water is a rectangle.* Teal spans x=248 to x=343 at every scanline from y=0 to y\u2248185 \u2014 the left edge does not deviate by one pixel over 185 rows \u2014 and it terminates at y=185 in a dead-straight horizontal cut with no bank, no lip, no transition tile. Dirt simply begins.\n\nSupporting: the two crates at x 64\u2013112 are pixel-identical including the diamond blot in the same corner of each lid; the barrels are the same sprite with the same 2 px cream rim and the same notch on the lid; nothing but the figure casts a shadow; and the frame is uniformly lit \u2014 mean luma per 96\u00d796 block runs 60.1 to 79.5 corner to corner, i.e. no falloff at all, in a scene whose premise is one carried lamp. The bones at x\u2248215\u2013245 are a scatter of pale cream dots with no silhouette and no dark under-pixel.",
  "FLAGGED": "1, 2, 3",
  "RANK": "3 > 2 > 1",
  "BEST": "3",
